All these linear transformations can be written at once as $X'^{\mu}=\Lambda^{\mu}{}_{
u}X^{
u}.$ The repeated index $
u$ is summed over $1,2,3,0$. This is simply the usual row-by-column sum in matrix multiplication, expressed in index notation.

