  B'^{\sigma}=\Lambda^\sigma{}_{	au}B^	au,$ then their product transforms as $A'^{\mu}B'^{\sigma}
  =\Lambda^\mu{}_{
u}\Lambda^\sigma{}_{	au}
   A^
u B^	au.$ This gives the defining law for a contravariant rank-two tensor: $T'^{\mu\sigma}
  =\Lambda^\mu{}_{
u}\Lambda^\sigma{}_{	au}T^{
u	au}.$ There is one Lorentz matrix for each index. The repeated $
u$ and $	au$ are summed; the open $\mu$ and $\sigma$ label the component being calculated in the primed frame.

